.TH OTPCLIENT 1 "October 2026" "otpclient" "OTPClient Manual"
.SH NAME
otpclient \- GTK4 / libadwaita client for TOTP and HOTP one-time passwords
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B otpclient
[\fB\-\-start\-minimized\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B OTPClient
is a GTK4 / libadwaita application that generates Time-based (TOTP) and
HMAC-based (HOTP) one-time passwords. The encrypted token database is
stored on disk using AES-256-GCM with an Argon2id-derived key.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-start\-minimized
Start with the window hidden in the system tray instead of shown. The database
is left locked, so the first time the window is shown it asks for the password.
This affects the current launch only and does not change the
.I start-minimized
preference. It is ignored, with the window shown normally, when
.I minimize-to-tray
is off or no system tray was detected.
.I \-\-start\-minimised
is accepted as a spelling alias.
.SH FEATURES
.IP \(bu 3
TOTP and HOTP support.
.IP \(bu 3
Custom digits (4-10), period (1-120 s), and algorithm (SHA1, SHA256, SHA512).
.IP \(bu 3
Steam-style codes.
.IP \(bu 3
Manage multiple databases and switch between them.
.IP \(bu 3
Per-token grouping with filterable views, and group-wide rename and removal.
.IP \(bu 3
Select several tokens to assign a group, export or delete them; a bulk delete
can be undone.
.IP \(bu 3
Tokens that fail validation are kept aside and can be repaired or deleted from a
review dialog.
.IP \(bu 3
Import and export Aegis (plain or encrypted), AuthPro (plain or encrypted),
2FAS (plain or encrypted), FreeOTP+ (plain), and Google Authenticator QR
codes (file or live capture). An import lists its tokens first, with exact
duplicates unchecked, so only the ones you keep are added.
.IP \(bu 3
Add new tokens manually, by scanning a QR code from a file, or via the
device camera.
.IP \(bu 3
Auto-lock after a configurable inactivity timeout, on screensaver
activation, or on demand.
.IP \(bu 3
Optional integration with the system Secret Service for keyring-stored
database passwords (also enables cross-database search).
.IP \(bu 3
Optional GNOME Shell / KDE KRunner search provider that surfaces tokens
in the system search results.
.SH TOKEN ACTIONS
Single-click and arrow keys select a token without generating or copying a code.
Each row carries a button in the Action column, copy for TOTP and generate for
HOTP, and the same action heads the row's right-click menu. Enter and Ctrl+C
activate the selected token while the token list has focus. Enter also activates
a search result.
HOTP counters are saved before the code is shown or copied. HOTP results from
another database open that database first.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.var/app/com.github.paolostivanin.OTPClient/config/otpclient/otpclient.cfg
Flatpak configuration file (when running under Flatpak).
.TP
.I ~/.config/otpclient/otpclient.cfg
Configuration file containing the path to the active database.
.TP
.I ~/.config/autostart/com.github.paolostivanin.OTPClient.desktop
Written when \fIStart at Login\fR is enabled in
.IR "Settings \-> Integration" .
Under Flatpak the same file is written on the host by
.IR org.freedesktop.portal.Background ,
which not every desktop implements; the setting is greyed out where it does not.
.TP
GSettings schema
.I com.github.paolostivanin.OTPClient
Stores user preferences (theme, auto-lock, notifications, KDF parameters, etc.).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Honoured by GLib for locating the configuration file.
